<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Canberra still mulling Air NZ's Ansett buy.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Canberra still mulling Air NZ's Ansett buy.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government's Foreign Investment Review Board is still considering Air New Zealand Ltd's application to buy 50 percent of airline Ansett Australia, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's still under consideration,&quot; the spokeswoman said, adding that the decision was legally required by September 26.</p>
<p>Earlier, Air New Zealand said it had agreed to buy TNT Ltd's 50 percent share of Ansett for A$475 million, including payments for TNT's subordinated debt in the airline and a capital contribution.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
